SCIENTIFIC INTERPRETATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Full-sample reproduction is treated as internal fidelity, not independent validation.
- Temporal validation calibrates only on 2020-2023 and evaluates 2024-2025.
- Validation-period outcomes do not determine temporal scenario thresholds.
- Previously selected probability families are not changed after seeing validation results.
- Low retains an empirical/nonparametric representation.
- Medium and High retain the previously authorized Lognormal family.
- DES validation uses only procedures with complete stage decomposition.
- K-S p-values are not interpreted as proof of distributional identity.
- Wasserstein distance and quantile errors complement hypothesis-test diagnostics.
- Monte Carlo iterations do not create additional independent tenders.
- DES simulated entities do not create additional independent tenders.
- No missing temporal values are imputed.
- No observations are removed from the master analytical population.
- No causal interpretation is authorized.

